# Fleet FIPS baseline: the OpenSSL majors a VE image may link, and the FIPS provider builds it may carry.
# Compiled into fips-invariant-check, so a new checker tag carries a new baseline, and Renovate
# (which tracks the checker version in every image repo) moves the whole fleet at once.
#
# Each image links exactly one OpenSSL core (rule 1), and its major follows that image's DU base.
# FIPS_OPENSSL_MAJORS lists the majors the fleet accepts. It holds both 3 and 4 while DU moves its
# bases to OpenSSL 4 unevenly; drop 3 once no base ships it. A major outside the list (a stray
# 1.1, a future 5) fails until someone adds it here deliberately.
#
# FIPS_PROVIDER_BUILDS lists BUILDINFO:CMVP pairs. Every provider module in an image (fips.so,
# fips-<version>.so) must report FIPS_PROVIDER_NAME and one of these builds; anything else fails.
#   3.4.0-r5:5132  what the fleet ships as fips.so (survey of deployed images, 2026-10-03). CMVP
#                  #5132's Security Policy names build 3.4.0-r4; the vendor has been asked.
#   3.6.0-r4:5523  DU's opt-in fips-3.6.0.so (newest bases, e.g. python-fips v3.14.8), whose
#                  build matches its Security Policy.
# Which provider is ACTIVE depends on the runtime OpenSSL config and is not checked here.
FIPS_OPENSSL_MAJORS="3 4"
FIPS_PROVIDER_NAME="Chainguard FIPS Provider for OpenSSL"
FIPS_PROVIDER_BUILDS="3.4.0-r5:5132 3.6.0-r4:5523"
